00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.640
by putting all the zeros inside,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:24.360
using a clock cycle. So basically on clock we put all the zeros in. So a useful function is clear

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:51.210
and that means synchronously put all zeros in entire registers, sorry, in all flip-flops.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:02:11.820
so that is... so we are going to create a register and we are going to have it be

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:27.180
a 2-bit multi-functional register that is going to have load and clear signals.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:44.110
Load is going to be designated as signal with LD, clear is going to be FCL and we

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:53.070
are also going to have a third function that is going to be called keep the current value.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:03:00.750
So let us make something that is called function table and keep is keeping the previous or current

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:18.290
value. So here is the functional table we are going to have two signals one is clear

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:29.330
CLR and LD and on 0,0 of all of them, both of them, we are going to have a function keep

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:41.080
the previous value. On 1,1 we are again going to keep the previous value. However, on 0,1

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:45.800
